## SEVERITY / VERDICT (decided HERE)
*Blocker:* a path outside the one; a product byte; a removed or reworded `expect(`, `toBe(`, `toEqual(`, `toBeGreaterThan(`, title, selector or positive control; a forbidden token (list in Step 1) added; a raised timeout or a retry; a row that is red from the head at no lag; lint, typecheck, build, `audit-dev`, `check-shards` or the two shards red from the head; a secret; non-ASCII or a person's name in an added line or the message. *Major:* a wait satisfied before the content a row reads is on the screen (a lag shows it); a frame other than documents with a call in flight at return; the documents reasoning failing at source (an element a row reads changes when that call answers); a builder claim your numbers contradict (red counts before, green counts after, the seconds, the shard counts); a required plant red-stays-green or the reverse (P3 excepted by reason); the instrument not firing at the base; the projected shard minutes above the main median or file seconds slower at the head. *Minor:* a redundant wait condition (green when removed, with the reason); a vacuous `toHaveCount(0)` with no positive condition after it; a plant of yours green in every row with no reason (missing check, with the cell). *Note:* the subject is 104 characters (the squash subject is yours, at most 100); `frame()`'s `ready` is required and `width` moved (the ticket said keep the optional argument); the other four specs that still sleep are not this branch's; main's `prototype-tablet-2` took 18.0 min (90 percent of 20) on one run: a Note for Tuesday; e2e shards other than the two, dotnet, SQL Server, hosted CI and CodeQL NOT RUN; UAT held, not touched. **GO** = steps 0-7 measured, nothing above Note; **GO WITH FINDINGS** = Minor/Note only; **NO GO** on any Blocker or Major.

